<title>FRANCE: Algeria, Turkish firms set up joint cement company.</title>
<headline>Algeria, Turkish firms set up joint cement company.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian and Turkish firms have set up a joint company to plan and build a terminal to distribute cement from within the port of Bejaia, 190 km (120 miles) east of Algiers, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The joint company, known as Mediterranean Cements (Ciments de Mediterranee) with a capital of $2 million, has been created by the Algerian Trading Cement Society and Turkey's Can Dis Ticaret Anonim Sirketi.</p>
</text>
